  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 126 PM EDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\n***** MONDAY - SATURDAY *****\n\nSlightly below normal temperatures, numerous clouds, and pop up \nafternoon showers are forecast to continue through at least Tuesday \nas the upper level cut-off low spins overhead. By Wednesday or \nThursday, a northern stream wave should lift that pesky resident low \ninto the Mid-Atlantic/Northeast, allowing a more seasonably humid \nand warm airmass to return to the region. Embedded within the \nrelatively zonal flow regime will likely be one or more shortwaves \ncapable of generating showers and storms (possibly severe), but \npredictability in terms of impacts and timing is low at this \njuncture. The forecast maintains slight (20-30%) chances for storms \nthrough next weekend while high temperatures, climbing a few degrees \neach day, reach the upper 80s to low 90s by Friday-Saturday.",
